#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-auto-connection.md:2
msgid "Interface auto-connection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-auto-connection.md:4
msgid ""
"Interfaces allow (or deny) access to a resource outside of a snap’s "
"confinement, but they're also designed to be convenient for users."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-auto-connection.md:6
msgid ""
"Part of this convenience is whether an interface is permitted to be "
"automatically connected when a snap is installed, or whether a snap can "
"request to include certain super-privileged interfaces to begin with. This "
"is the auto-connection mechanism."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-auto-connection.md:8
msgid "Auto-connections"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-auto-connection.md:10
msgid ""
"The snapd interface auto-connection mechanism has been designed to remove "
"the need for a manual connection when:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-auto-connection.md:12
msgid ""
"An interface is commonly required and has no or minor security implications"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-auto-connection.md:13
msgid ""
"A snap provides, or accesses, libraries or other content vital to the "
"operation of the snap"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-auto-connection.md:14
msgid "There is a need to connect snaps that are designed to work together"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-auto-connection.md:15
msgid ""
"Store-set policy applies to let a given snap use an interface that would not "
"be generally auto-connected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-auto-connection.md:17
msgid ""
"See {ref}`Process for aliases, auto-connections and tracks <interfaces-"
"process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks>` for details on how to "
"submit an auto-connection is requested ."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-auto-connection.md:19
msgid ""
"If a snap is installed prior to an interface being granted auto-connect "
"permission, and permission is subsequently granted and the snap updated, "
"when the installed snap updates, the interface will be auto-connected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-auto-connection.md:21
msgid "Auto-connection process"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-auto-connection.md:23
msgid ""
"Whenever a snap is installed or refreshed, snapd will review its unconnected "
"plugs and their candidate slots for auto-connection potential. It does the "
"same for its slots and candidate plugs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-auto-connection.md:25
msgid ""
"If there is exactly one candidate slot for a plug then an interface "
"connection is automatically performed. The requirement for exactly one "
"candidate can be changed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-auto-connection.md:27
msgid ""
"For an interface, the candidate plug and slot pairs are determined using "
"constraints-based rules. The rule language can either express allowing or "
"denying an auto-connection, with the latter taking precedence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-auto-connection.md:29
msgid ""
"Rules are either built-in to snapd or conveyed via assertions (signed "
"documents) that correspond to a given snap (snap-declarations). The rules "
"are scoped and attached to the slot or plug side of an interface at either "
"one of those two levels:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-auto-connection.md:31
msgid "the built-in level"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-auto-connection.md:32
msgid "the snap level"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-auto-connection.md:34
msgid ""
"To simplify reasoning about their effect, the rules from the different "
"levels/scopes are not merged but rather prioritised according to level:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-auto-connection.md:36
msgid "snap plug (from the snap-declaration of the snap with the plug)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-auto-connection.md:37
msgid "snap slot (from the snap-declaration of the snap sporting the slot)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-auto-connection.md:38
msgid "built-in plug level"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-auto-connection.md:39
msgid "built-in slot level"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-auto-connection.md:41
msgid ""
"From snap plug to the built-in slot level, it’s the level that first "
"provides any rules that determines the rules used and considered. This "
"ordering reflects a scale from the most specific usage perspective, snap "
"plug side consumption, to the most general, builtin slot rules."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-auto-connection.md:43
msgid ""
"Built-in rules embody the general policy of whether and when an interface "
"should be auto-connected, and as such, these are documented with the "
"interface. Consequently, snap-declaration rules express store-set policy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-auto-connection.md:45
msgid ""
"A user can also issue \"snap connect\" and \"snap disconnect\" commands. In "
"particular, a manual \"snap disconnect\" of an auto-connection will inhibit "
"a subsequent refresh from re-establishing the auto-connection (unless the "
"manual disconnect overrides this default behaviour using the \"--forget\" "
"option)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-auto-connection.md:47
msgid "Auto-connection constraints"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-auto-connection.md:49
msgid ""
"The following is an example built-in auto-connection rule (attached to the "
"slot-side) for the content interface:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-auto-connection.md:51
msgid ""
"slots:\n"
"  content:\n"
"    allow-auto-connection:\n"
"      plug-publisher-id:\n"
"        - $SLOT_PUBLISHER_ID\n"
"      plug-attributes:\n"
"        content: $SLOT(content)\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-auto-connection.md:61
msgid "The above example permits an auto-connection if:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-auto-connection.md:63
msgid "the publisher of both the slot and plug side snaps is the same"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-auto-connection.md:64
msgid "the \"content\" attribute on the plug and slot match"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-auto-connection.md:66
msgid ""
"The rule language allows us to deny or allow auto-connections with the "
"following constraints:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-auto-connection.md:68
msgid ""
"attributes values on the plug and slot (based on regular expressions or "
"special expressions like $SLOT(content) in the example)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-auto-connection.md:69
msgid "snap type or the snap-id of the plug or slot snap"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-auto-connection.md:70
msgid "publisher of the slot or plug snap"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-auto-connection.md:71
msgid "actual names of the plug or slot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-auto-connection.md:72
msgid "whether the device is a classic system or not"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-auto-connection.md:73
msgid "the actual store in use or device model (for IoT use-cases)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-auto-connection.md:75
msgid ""
"Further lists of constraints or values can be used in the rule language to "
"express alternation (logical OR)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-auto-connection.md:78
msgid ""
"The same language rules can be used to define rules other than interface "
"auto-connections, including default policy for ordinary connections and "
"installations, and to override policy for the more sensitive interfaces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-auto-connection.md:81
msgid "Auto-connection with a default-provider"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-auto-connection.md:83
msgid ""
"A content interface plug can specify a default-provider. This is the name of "
"a snap that can be installed to fulfil the plug's need. If there isn’t a "
"slot with the content label of the plug on the system the specified snap "
"will be installed before the snap with the plug. However, if there is a slot "
"on the system that already has the content label, any default-provider "
"specified by a content interface plug is ignored. If the specified snap is "
"already installed but there is no slot with the content label, the specified "
"snap will be upgraded instead under the assumption that a newer version may "
"start providing the label."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-auto-connection.md:85
msgid ""
"The default-provider mechanism triggers the installation or upgrade of the "
"provider snap as described but it does not include an implied connection. "
"The auto-connection will only happen by means of and if it is permitted by "
"the general auto-connection mechanism."
msgstr ""
